.ignore
package-lock.json
# ...except the dashboard's: it is deployed, so its build has to be reproducible. Without the lock
# in git, every machine resolves its own dependency tree from the same package.json — the deploy
# host, CI and each developer end up on different versions, and an `npm audit` result describes one
# machine on one day rather than the commit. Deploy installs it with `npm ci`, which reads the lock
# and never rewrites it (plain `npm i` would, leaving the tree dirty and breaking the next
# `git pull`). The examples under wasi-examples/ stay ignored — they are samples, not deployments.
!dashboard/package-lock.json
.research
multi-keystore-research.md
cloudflare-account-migration.md
